NLP Approach: Ingesting the UK Labour Market
* The Alternative Data Asset: Processed a comprehensive dataset of 62.3 million raw UK job advertisements spanning a 6-year period to identify the labour driving "own-account" data creation.
* Text Standardisation: Executed rigorous cleaning protocols to strip out grammatical stop words, remove special characters, and convert the entire text corpus to lowercase.
* Noun Chunk Extraction: Deployed spaCy natural language processing to extract complete grammatical phrases rather than isolated single words, preserving critical technical context (e.g., "relational database management" instead of "database").
* Initial Scale: This extraction phase expanded the raw job adverts into a gross dataset of approximately 8.7 billion individual noun chunks awaiting statistical evaluation.
