NLP Approach: The Mathematical Filtration Engine
* 0.35 Semantic Boundary: Mapped phrases into a 300-dimensional vector space using cosine similarity, permanently filtering out unrelated jargon by requiring a strict mathematical proximity to the core concept of "data".
* 10.0x Relative Share Multiplier: Eliminated generic office buzzwords by demanding that a technical phrase appear at least 10 times more frequently in specialised Anchor Occupations (e.g., Data Entry - SOC 4114) than in the baseline UK economy.
* 0.45 Gold Standard Polish: Required surviving terms to achieve a high semantic similarity to undeniable, verified baseline pillars (e.g., CRM, ERP, data records).
* The Classification Gate: Scanned the 62.3 million adverts against the final verified dictionary. A role was only classified as a "Data-Intensive Job" if it contained at least 3 distinct terms from the lexicon.
