NLP Approach: Macroeconomic Mapping & Valuation
* Bridging the Structural Gap: Job advertisements are inherently categorised by Occupational codes (SOC), whereas National Accounts require Industry codes (SIC).
* Probabilistic Crosswalk Matrix: Engineered a mathematical distribution model using census demographic weights to reallocate the identified data workforce from their SOC groups into their actual operating industry sectors.
* Applying the Sum-of-Costs: Linked the SIC-mapped data workers to ONS Supply and Use Tables to isolate their specific Compensation of Employees (base wages).
* Capital Valuation: Applied sector-specific Alpha ($\alpha$) markups to the isolated wages to account for physical overhead, software tools, and operating surplus, culminating in an absolute macroeconomic valuation of UK data assets.
